    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (77.94) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) serving as our primary offensive catalysts. **Corbin Carroll** remains an auto-start despite facing a pitcher with a 53% SB hold rate; his elite speed profile against the matchup with Holmes keeps his ceiling high, while **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment that vaults him into elite territory. **Josh Naylor** (70.81) is our strongest utilization of the platoon advantage; facing Kay, he benefits from a 19% SP skill boost and favorable wind-out conditions, making him a cornerstone of today\u2019s projected scoring.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Zach McKinstry** (49.17) on the bench. While his profile against Wacha offered some upside, he ultimately fell behind the floor set by **Alex Freeland** and **Dalton Rushing**. Though we are monitoring pending lineups for both **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**, their ability to capitalize on Strider\u2019s 4.71 xERA\u2014specifically the +17% SP skill boost\u2014outweighed the marginal gains offered by **Zach McKinstry** or **Austin Riley**. **Austin Riley** remains on the bench primarily due to a tough draw against Snell, which suppressed his efficiency score to 48.69. \n\nWe are tracking a few situational variables: while **Jose Caballero** (60.22) looks excellent against Harrison due to a 13% platoon edge, we are keeping a close eye on the bench, where **Travis Bazzana** (41.35) remains available but faces a 45% rain risk, justifying his exclusion today. We expect **James Wood** to provide a solid baseline (62.17) from the leadoff spot; his 0.379 xwOBA is a key metric we are banking on to drive our total runs and RBI totals higher, provided he can navigate his matchup against Junk.",
